        "original_id": "e4fee065-8ef3-5a69-a4aa-79ceee52543a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Atlanta, Georgia, USA; southeastern United States; downtown; Vine City\n- Organizations: Georgia World Congress Center Authority; State of Georgia\n- Systems: Georgia World Congress Center\n- Products: Georgia Dome; Mercedes-Benz Stadium; Centennial Olympic Park\n- Events: Southeastern Flower Show\n\nFacts:\n- The Georgia World Congress Center is a convention center in Atlanta, Georgia, USA.\n- The Southeastern Flower Show is held in early spring in Atlanta, Georgia, at the Georgia World Congress Center.\n- The Georgia World Congress Center Authority later developed the Georgia Dome, Centennial Olympic Park, and Mercedes-Benz Stadium.\n- Mercedes-Benz Stadium replaced the Georgia Dome.\n- The Georgia Dome is a recently retired domed stadium in the southeastern United States and is currently under demolition.\n- The Georgia Dome is located in Atlanta, Georgia, between downtown to the east and Vine City to the west.\n- The State of Georgia owned and operated the Georgia Dome as part of the Georgia World Congress Center Authority.",
